 "title": "La Pola and her compatriots",
 "hook": "During Colombia’s struggle for independence, Royalists executed scores of women by shooting squad, the most famous of whom was the seamstress and spy known as “La Pola.” Writing last year for the cultural journal of Colombia’s central bank, historian Pablo Rodríguez Jiménez presented a list of 76 women known to have suffered this fate — their names, locations, and dates of death.",
